{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 31,
  "title": "The beach",
  "description": "Name the things on a beach, and say where they are.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "The beach has its own small set of nouns, and most of them are feminine. The plural is worth noticing, because one of them loses its ending.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The nouns",
        "body": "La orilla, la arena, la ola, la concha, la sombrilla, la espuma, la roca and el castillo de arena are feminine. El bañador and el cubo are masculine. El castillo de arena is a whole phrase, and it takes el like other masculine nouns.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "la arena",
            "en": "the sand"
          },
          {
            "es": "la ola",
            "en": "the wave"
          },
          {
            "es": "el castillo de arena",
            "en": "the sandcastle"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "At the edge of the sea",
        "body": "La orilla is where the water meets the sand. You say a thing is at the edge with en la orilla, and inside the water with en el agua. One word is special: la concha becomes las conchas in the plural, but el cubo becomes los cubos.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "las olas están malas",
            "en": "the waves are bad"
          },
          {
            "es": "la sombrilla está en la arena",
            "en": "the parasol is on the sand"
          },
          {
            "es": "los niños están en el agua",
            "en": "the children are in the water"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
